The legal texts are official texts of the Republic of Moldova (the Constitution of 29 July 1994 as amended,
and the Constitutional Court judgment HCC7/2016), as published by the State Register of Legal Acts in its
earlier home lex.justice.md (Ministry of Justice), read through Internet Archive captures, and in the Moldpres
edition "Constituția Republicii Moldova. Cu modificări și completări la data de 20 octombrie 2024" (PDF hosted
at presedinte.md), retrieved 29 October 2026. Official documents such as laws and court decisions are not
objects of copyright under Law 139/2010 on copyright and related rights.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph or
lettered point per line; typesetting was normalised (cedilla and comma-below s/t as one letter, spaced dashes,
spacing, letter-spaced headings, line-end hyphens of the PDF); the register's notes and footnotes were left out;
the Constitutional Court's judgment was applied to the articles it names; and the versions were arranged as git
commits credited to the acts that made each change. The wording of the law was not changed. Neither the State
Register, Moldpres nor the Presidency endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
